            "author": "betteraitips",
            "region": "US",
            "shares": 16,
            "caption": "AI agents can now negotiate on your behalf in real time. This guy handed his phone to a stranger on Craigslist and let ChatGPT handle the whole deal. The AI talked him down from $10,000. It was patient, polite, and persistent. It also agreed to $400 for a loaf of bread. That gap between impressive and dangerous is exactly where AI agents live right now. The capability is real. The judgment is not always there. And most people have no idea how close we are to AI making purchases for us without asking first. Before you hand over that kind of trust, you need to understand what these agents actually do when left alone. Follow @BetterAITips for more AI breakdowns like this. Would you let an AI negotiate or buy something on your behalf today? Credits: 📽️ Video: AI Bread Negotiation | @husk.irl",
